## 🧠 Reflection

Day 14 made me realize that declarative development on Salesforce requires just as much architectural discipline as writing programmatic Apex code. It is incredibly easy to drag and drop elements on the Flow canvas to solve an immediate problem, but without strict governance rules, those quick fixes quickly compound into a messy, unmanageable technical debt.

The most valuable takeaway from today was learning how to implement robust fault paths. Building a flow that not only succeeds along the happy path but can gracefully catch database failures and document detailed error messaging changes the dynamic completely. Combining rigorous branching logic with an organized 1-Flow-per-Object design strategy gives me a highly reliable framework to scale complex enterprise automations safely.
